To ensure that the minimum exposure area ( S 
                         min 
                         )  immersed in solution larger than 1000 mm 2 , the dimensions of specimens used in immersion test are 50 × 25 × 2 mm, which is in accordance with standards of ASTM  G31  [ 43 ] and JB/T 6073-1992 [ 44 ]. To remove the oxide on the surface and to ensure the post-polished working surface, the specimen was mechanically grounded by SiC abrasive papers from 200 # to 2000 #. Then, the specimen was immersed in 3.5 wt% NaCl solution for 4, 7, and 10 days.
